# What `flutter pub publish` leaves out of the package.
#
# A .pubignore replaces the .gitignore of its folder for pub: with this file,
# pub no longer reads the root .gitignore, so its rules are repeated here. Keep
# the two in sync. Pub still reads the .gitignore files of subfolders (example/
# and its platform runners), and always skips dotfiles, dot-directories
# (.github/, .dart_tool/, .idea/), pubspec.lock and pubspec_overrides.yaml.

# Build output: `flutter test` creates build/ at the root (75+ MB), and
# example/build/ comes from running the example. `build/` matches both.
build/
.dart_tool/
coverage/
doc/api/

# IDE files (pub skips the dot-directories anyway)
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/

# Agent and contributor docs. llms.txt ships on purpose.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Images that no file in this version uses. The READMEs of earlier versions on
# pub.dev load them from GitHub, so they stay in the repository. The current
# README loads its images from GitHub too; the package only needs the files
# that `screenshots:` in pubspec.yaml lists.
assets/dark_mode_animation.gif
assets/flutter_settings_ui_logo.png
assets/navigation-tile.png
assets/settings-list.png
assets/settings-section.png
assets/simple-tile.png
assets/switch-tile.png
assets/v2/android/
assets/v2/iOS/
